  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math> be two non-null events such that <math><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8834;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> Then, which of the following statements is always correct?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lGCOm",
      "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≥</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Hxf3f",
      "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OCePE",
      "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>≤</mo><mi> </mi><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "CJo6x",
      "text": "<math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lets draw the venn diagram according to question,&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/98480e4a-e9de-4d95-91f0-324fe32c9477-image6.png\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8201;</mo><mo>&#8201;</mo><mo>&#8201;</mo><mo>&#8201;</mo><mo>&#8201;</mo><mo>&#8201;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8834;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8745;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>]</mo></math></p><p>Now, since <math><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>|</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>",
